  "tsb_template": {
    "prompt": "Edit this drone image. It is the layout of a compact quadcopter for everyday aerial photography, in a strict orthographic top view with the nose toward the top edge. Turn it into the finished product. Keep the four motor centres, the arm directions and the length of the propeller blades exactly as they are in the image{body}. The two blades of each propeller are identical in length and width and point in exactly opposite directions from the hub, never a V shape. No propeller guards.\n{rest}",
    "body": ", and keep the width of the central body exactly as it is in the image",
    "rest": "The nose points to the top edge of the image. The rear end of the fuselage is a closed, plain light grey shell: no dark part, opening, camera or module at the tail.\nA rounded pod with a continuous curved outline.\nEach arm grows out of the shell through a smooth seamless blend, with no joint line at the root.\nThe camera sits inside the nose, flush with the shell; from directly overhead only a thin dark strip of its front window shows at the very front edge of the nose. The camera faces horizontally forward.\nA plain top cover with no seams crossing it.\nArms in the same matte light grey as the shell.\nMatte light grey shell and arms in one continuous colour, dark grey motors, black propellers.\nShow the complete product on a plain light background. Omit guide marks and lettering.",
    "cfg": 3,
    "rule": "输入为同号两段式第一步的原图，不裁不改；种子与第一步相同；其余与 WLQ 请求相同"
  }
